  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- Fixed: `StringCE.RemoveLinesWhere` and `StringIndenter.IndentToDepth` split a string at every line ending, LF and CRLF alike, and end the lines they return in `Environment.NewLine`. They split only at `Environment.NewLine`, so on Windows, text from a raw string literal in a package compiled on Linux, whose lines end in LF, was one line to them: Compze.Must's failure messages showed the placeholder for a line to leave out, `RemoveLine`, and Compze.Internals.Logging's exception messages, which indent with `IndentToDepth`, indented only their first line of such text.",
